{
  "scenario_id": "sim-hospital-life-safety-ride-through",
  "title": "Hospital: life-safety ride-through and med-gas manifold upgrade",
  "description": "Two independent branches behind a 2N source pair: the life-safety branch (ATS -> LS panel -> OR air handlers and med gas) and the general branch (UPS -> PDU -> general panel -> imaging and general HVAC). A utility fault drops the general branch while life-safety services ride through on the generator — the ride-through adjudicated exactly, including that no asset's single fault can reach OR air. The generator faulting alone is loss-invisible. A lone med-gas manifold (N) fails and interrupts medical gas; its repair restores it; upgrading the manifold to N+1 (standby added) removes the SPOF; the primary then fails again and the standby absorbs it, with the report honestly degrading tolerance (first_fault_tolerated flips false, the standby becomes the SPOF). Adjudicates Categories 1 and 2 for hospitals plus the redundancy-change surface M3's what-if claims will build on.",
  "market": "hospital",
